Title:
Aether — Self-mutating macOS implant (runtime mutation/metamorphism PoC)

Type:
GitHub Tool

Short Summary (4-8 sentences max):
Aether is a macOS (x86_64/ARM64) proof-of-concept implant focused on runtime mutation/metamorphism at the instruction level. It rewrites its own executable code in memory to evade static analysis while preserving program semantics. The project emphasizes native-only operation using Mach-O manipulation and macOS APIs, and includes in-memory encryption plus a “dead-drop” style C2 concept. It’s explicitly positioned as research-only and noted as still behaviorally detectable, but modular enough to extend with custom stealth, C2, or persistence. Useful primarily for red team tradecraft R&D, malware research, and defenders studying metamorphic techniques on macOS.

Technical Focus:
- Instruction-level metamorphism / runtime self-modifying code
- Mach-O parsing and in-memory code rewriting
- Native macOS API usage (no external frameworks)
- In-memory encryption of payload/code/data
- Dead-drop command-and-control design
- Cross-architecture support (x86_64 and ARM64)

Use Cases:
- Researching macOS metamorphic/self-modifying implant techniques
- Building or extracting a mutation engine for custom loaders/implants
- Testing static-analysis resilience and reverse-engineering workflows
- Developing detections for runtime code mutation and Mach-O tampering
- Prototyping dead-drop C2 patterns for low-interaction command retrieval

Keywords:
macOS, Mach-O, metamorphism, polymorphism, self-modifying code, runtime mutation, instruction rewriting, in-memory encryption, dead-drop C2, implant, native APIs, x86_64, ARM64, static analysis evasion, behavioral detection, code cave, loader, malware research, reverse engineering, red team R&D